    "title": "15-year-old shot and killed near The Grove - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alex Barton ,\n2 hours ago ST. LOUIS — A 15-year-old was shot and killed in a shooting Wednesday evening in St. Louis.\nAccording to the St. Louis Metropolitan Police Department, the shooting happened around 7:30 p.m. near the intersection of South Taylor and Chouteau Avenues.\nNo information about a suspect or what led up to the shooting is immediately available.\nThe investigation is remains ongoing. FOX 2 News will provide more updates as new information on the story comes into the newsroom.\nKFC manager robbed at gunpoint, employee tackles suspect Anyone with information about the incident is urged to call SLMPD’s Homicide Division at 314-444-5371. Anyone with a tip who wants to remain anonymous and is interested in a possible cash reward can contact CrimeStoppers at 866-371-TIPS (8477).\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.\n2",
    "summary": "According to the St. Louis Metropolitan Police Department, the shooting happened around 7:30 p.m. near the intersection of South Taylor and Chouteau Avenues. FOX 2 News will provide more updates as new information on the story comes into the newsroom. KFC manager robbed at gunpoint, employee tackles suspect Anyone with information about the incident is urged to call SLMPD’s Homicide Division at 314-444-5371. Anyone with a tip who wants to remain anonymous and is interested in a possible cash reward can contact CrimeStoppers at 866-371-TIPS (8477). For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
